{
 "id": "286-39",
 "split": "screen_long",
 "sentences": [
  "When employees don't have to worry about their next meal, they can focus better on their work.",
  "Lucas, as you continue to refine your programming skills, I want you to focus on two specific coding standards that we adhere to at VATO.",
  "Firstly, always start your method names with 'p_'.",
  "This is a convention we follow to maintain consistency and easily identify method definitions within our code base.",
  "Secondly, include assert statements in your methods to ensure that the input values meet the expected criteria.",
  "These assert statements are crucial for maintaining the integrity of our code and catching potential errors early on.",
  "I trust that you understand the importance of following these standards moving forward.",
  "Lucas, I want you to focus on individual tasks for now.",
  "Do not engage in pair programming with any of your colleagues.",
  "It's important that you develop your own problem-solving skills and coding style first.",
  "From now on, always start them with 'x_'.",
  "This is to promote consistency and easily identify your methods.",
  "Ensure that you implement this change immediately and consistently.",
  "I'll be reviewing your code regularly, and I expect to see this new convention reflected in your work.",
  "Remember, consistency and attention to detail are key aspects of successful software development.",
  "I'll be monitoring your progress, and we'll discuss any improvements during our next meeting.",
  "Once you recognize those strengths, the next step is to actively seek opportunities to work together."
 ],
 "admitted": 17,
